## 5. Clinical content — request (N)

5.1 Encoding rules
5.1.1 JSON SHALL be UTF-8, RFC 8259, no comments
5.1.2 Object key uniqueness, ordering, NaN/Inf prohibited
5.1.3 Numeric, string, and identifier limits
5.1.4 Forward-compatible "ignore unknown fields" rule
5.2 `SmartHealthCheckinRequest` (top level)
5.2.1 `type` (fixed discriminator)
5.2.2 `version`
5.2.3 `id` (SHALL be unique per requester per session; recommended entropy)
5.2.4 `purpose` (display, not identity)
5.2.5 `fhirVersions[]`
5.2.6 `items[]`
5.2.7 Prohibited fields (requester identity metadata)
5.2.8 (EX) minimal request, full request
5.3 `SmartHealthCheckinRequestItem`
5.3.1 `id` uniqueness, allowed character set
5.3.2 `title`
5.3.3 `summary`
5.3.4 `required` semantics (advisory only; user always controls)
5.3.5 `accept[]` (ordered preference)
5.3.6 `content` (selector — see §5.4)
5.4 Content selectors (`content.kind`)
5.4.1 `fhir.resources`
5.4.1.1 `profiles[]` — exact StructureDefinition canonicals
5.4.1.2 `profilesFrom[]` — IG / publication / profile-collection canonical URLs
5.4.1.3 `resourceTypes[]` — official FHIR resource type names
5.4.1.4 Additivity rule when both `profiles` and `profilesFrom` present
5.4.1.5 No-selector default ("any patient-specific FHIR")
5.4.1.6 (EX) US Core family, exact CARIN coverage, mixed
5.4.2 `questionnaire`
5.4.2.1 By canonical
5.4.2.2 Inline `Questionnaire`
5.4.2.3 Combined canonical+resource
5.4.2.4 Wallet behavior when both forms supplied disagree
5.4.2.5 (EX) inline migraine intake
5.4.3 Extension selectors — registration rules
5.5 Canonical `|version` handling (decision matrix)
5.5.1 Strip vs. preserve table (one row per operation)
5.5.2 Round-trip preservation requirement on returned `meta.profile` and `QuestionnaireResponse.questionnaire`
5.6 Accepted media types (`accept[]`)
5.6.1 `application/fhir+json`
5.6.2 `application/smart-health-card`
5.6.3 Extension media types — registration rules
5.6.4 `accept` ordering semantics

